                    "Citation": "Poulsen ME et al; Anal Bioanal Chem 389 (6): 1799-804 (2007)",
                    "Matched": {
                      "PCLID": 26827323,
                      "Citation": "Poulsen ME, Christensen HB, Sørensen MT, Leffers H, Andersen JH. Determination of chlormequat in pig serum and sow milk by LC–MS/MS. Analytical and Bioanalytical Chemistry. 2007 Sep 12;389(6):1799–804. doi: 10.1007/s00216-007-1457-y.",
                      "PMID": 17849106,
                      "DOI": "10.1007/s00216-007-1457-y"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "Value": {
                  "StringWithMarkup": [
                    {
                      "String": "A LC-MS/MS method for the analysis of chlormequat in milk and serum was developed and validated ... Validation of the method was based on recovery tests at three spiking levels, determined as double determinations and repeated at least four times. Samples were extracted with methanol-water-acetic acid, centrifuged, filtrated and determined by LC-MS/MS. The mean recoveries were in the range 80-110%, and the LOD was 0.2 ng/g for serum and 0.3 ng/g for milk...",
                      "Markup": [
                        {
                          "Start": 38,
                          "Length": 11,
                          "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/chlormequat",
                          "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
