                        "Matched": {
                          "PCLID": 906297336,
                          "Citation": "U.S. Environmental Protection Agency. 1998. Extremely Hazardous Substances (EHS) Chemical Profiles and Emergency First Aid Guides. Washington, D.C.: U.S. Government Printing Office."
                        }
                      }
                    ],
                    "Value": {
                      "StringWithMarkup": [
                        {
                          "String": "Signs and Symptoms of Chlormequat Chloride Exposure: No information on specific clinical effects of exposure to chlormequat chloride was found in available references. However, because chlormequat chloride is expected to be corrosive, irritation and burning of the skin, eyes, and mucous membranes may be noted. Light-headedness, drowsiness, slurred speech, pupillary dilation, increased salivation, dysphagia (difficulty swallowing), abdominal pain, and spontaneous vomiting may occur. Stridor (high pitched, noisy respirations), dyspnea (shortness of breath), and pulmonary edema may occur. Apathy and mental confusion may develop, with progression to coma and death.",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 22,
                              "Length": 20,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/Chlormequat%20Chloride",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "CID-13836"
                            },
                            {
                              "Start": 112,
                              "Length": 20,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/chlormequat%20chloride",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "CID-13836"
                            },
                            {
                              "Start": 185,
                              "Length": 20,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/chlormequat%20chloride",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "CID-13836"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "Emergency Life-Support Procedures: Acute exposure to chlormequat chloride may require decontamination and life support for the victims. Emergency personnel should wear protective clothing appropriate to the type and degree of contamination. Air-purifying or supplied-air respiratory equipment should also be worn, as necessary. Rescue vehicles should carry supplies such as plastic sheeting and disposable plastic bags to assist in preventing spread of contamination.",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 53,
                              "Length": 20,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/chlormequat%20chloride",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "CID-13836"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "Inhalation Exposure:"
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "1. Move victims to fresh air. Emergency personnel should avoid self-exposure to chlormequat chloride.",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 80,
                              "Length": 20,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/chlormequat%20chloride",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "CID-13836"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "2. Evaluate vital signs including pulse and respiratory rate, and note any trauma. If no pulse is detected, provide CPR. If not breathing, provide artificial respiration. If breathing is labored, administer oxygen or other respiratory support.",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 207,
                              "Length": 6,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/element/Oxygen",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "Element-Oxygen"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "3. Obtain authorization and/or further instructions from the local hospital for administration of an antidote or performance of other invasive procedures."
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "4. Rush to a health care facility."
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "Dermal/Eye Exposure:"
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "1. Remove victims from exposure. Emergency personnel should avoid self-exposure to chlormequat chloride.",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 83,
                              "Length": 20,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/chlormequat%20chloride",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "CID-13836"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "2. Evaluate vital signs including pulse and respiratory rate, and note any trauma. If no pulse is detected, provide CPR. If not breathing, provide artificial respiration. If breathing is labored, administer oxygen or other respiratory support.",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 207,
                              "Length": 6,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/element/Oxygen",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "Element-Oxygen"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "3. Remove and isolate contaminated clothing as soon as possible."
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "4. If eye exposure has occurred, eyes must be flushed with lukewarm water for at least 30 minutes.",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 68,
                              "Length": 5,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/water",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "CID-962"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "5. Wash exposed skin areas thoroughly with water.",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 43,
                              "Length": 5,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/water",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "CID-962"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "6. Obtain authorization and/or further instructions from the local hospital for administration of an antidote or performance of other invasive procedures."
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "7. Rush to a health care facility."
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "Ingestion Exposure:"
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "1. Evaluate vital signs including pulse and respiratory rate, and note any trauma. If no pulse is detected, provide CPR. If not breathing, provide artificial respiration. If breathing is labored, administer oxygen or other respiratory support.",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 207,
                              "Length": 6,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/element/Oxygen",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "Element-Oxygen"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "2. DO NOT induce vomiting or attempt to neutralize!"
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "3. Obtain authorization and/or further instructions from the local hospital for administration of an antidote or performance of other invasive procedures."
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "4. Activated charcoal is of no value.",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 13,
                              "Length": 8,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/charcoal",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "CID-5462310"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "5. Give the victims water or milk: children up to 1 year old, 125 mL (4 oz or 1/2 cup); children 1 to 12 years old, 200 mL (6 oz or 3/4 cup); adults, 250 mL (8 oz or 1 cup). Water or milk should be given only if victims are conscious and alert.",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 20,
                              "Length": 5,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/water",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "CID-962"
                            },
                            {
                              "Start": 174,
                              "Length": 5,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/Water",
                              "Type": "PubChem Internal Link",
                              "Extra": "CID-962"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "String": "6. Rush to a health care facility. (EPA, 1998)"
                        }
                      ]
