                          "Citation": "USEPA/Office of Pesticide Programs; Environmental Fate and Ecological Risk Assessment for the Reregistration of Chlormequat Chloride p.20 EPA-HQ-OPP-2007-0968-0002 (2007). Available from, as of October 27, 2008: https://www.epa.gov/pesticides/reregistration/status.htm"
                        }
                      }
                    ],
                    "Value": {
                      "StringWithMarkup": [
                        {
                          "String": "/BIRDS and MAMMALS/ /An/ ...avian reproduction study with the Japanese quail... had mean-measured concentrations of 158, 387 and 982 mg/kg diet. The study was conducted with a two week pre-treatment period followed by a 6-week exposure period, rather than the guideline 10-week pre-laying exposure followed by a 10-week egg-laying exposure period. The most sensitive endpoints were the adult parameters of food consumption and male body weight gain; both endpoints showed significant adverse effects at all treatment levels. As a result, the required NOAEC could not be statistically determined (<158 mg ai/kg diet) from this study. The most sensitive reproductive parameter was a significant reduction in hatchlings per eggs set and number of cracked eggs in the highest test concentration. Additionally, absolute testes weight was significantly reduced (by 16%) in the 982 mg/kg group and there was a significant increase in egg shell thinning and decreased egg strength at the highest test concentration. These reductions may reflect effects on endocrine-mediated processes."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "ReferenceNumber": 21,
                    "Description": "PEER REVIEWED",
                    "Reference": [
                      "USEPA/Office of Pesticide Programs; Environmental Fate and Ecological Risk Assessment for the Reregistration of Chlormequat Chloride p.7 EPA-HQ-OPP-2007-0968-0002 (2007). Available from, as of October 27, 2008: https://www.epa.gov/pesticides/reregistration/status.htm"
                    ],
                    "ExtendedReference": [
                      {
                        "Citation": "USEPA/Office of Pesticide Programs; Environmental Fate and Ecological Risk Assessment for the Reregistration of Chlormequat Chloride p.7 EPA-HQ-OPP-2007-0968-0002 (2007). Available from, as of October 27, 2008: https://www.epa.gov/pesticides/reregistration/status.htm",
                        "Matched": {
                          "PCLID": 900001737,
                          "Citation": "USEPA/Office of Pesticide Programs; Environmental Fate and Ecological Risk Assessment for the Reregistration of Chlormequat Chloride p.7 EPA-HQ-OPP-2007-0968-0002 (2007). Available from, as of October 27, 2008: https://www.epa.gov/pesticides/reregistration/status.htm"
                        }
                      }
                    ],
                    "Value": {
                      "StringWithMarkup": [
                        {
                          "String": "/AQUATIC SPECIES/ In a 21-day chronic toxicity study on the water flea, ...a NOAEC of 5.0 mg ai/L was reported based on a statistically significant 20% reduction in live offspring relative to the control.",
                          "Markup": [
